PASS G2b countercontrol: I(x)P+ + X(x)P- != CNOT
PASS G2c CNOT = [I(x)P+ + (-iZ)(x)P-][I(x)(P+ + iP-)], (P+ + iP-)^2 = X
PASS G2d Ad(I(x)(P+ + iP-)) = actT Rx(pi/2) on all 16 basis tables
PASS G3 delta(CNOT) = delta(I(x)(P+ + iP-)) = -1, delta(SU(2)(x)I) = +1; Ad(I(x)Rx(pi/2)) not in the connected part
PASS G4 word = N[I(x)P+] + (N V^-1 Z V Z)(x)P-; tr(V^-1ZVZ Z) = 0 (rotation axis in the XY plane), symbolic
PASS L1 Lie closure of su(2)(x)I and its CNOT conjugate: dim 6 = su(2)(x)P+ (+) su(2)(x)P-
PASS L2 Lie closure of I(x)su(2) and its CNOT conjugate: dim 6 = P0(x)su(2) (+) P1(x)su(2)
PASS L3 both closures are invariant under the level-(ii) generators Ad(I(x)Z), Ad(Z(x)I) and the transpose
PASS L4 countercontrol: commuting generator iZ(x)I closes at dim 1
